factorium-pointer-registry-v0
pointer action | Action | a structural label for what an actor, system, or process does or attempts
pointer actor | Actor | a structural label for a participant associated with an action
pointer assumptions | Assumptions | structural labels for declared premises or conditions accepted for a bounded analysis
pointer authority | Authority | a structural label for the source or scope of a legitimate decision or action right
pointer basis | Basis | a structural label for the declared foundation used to calculate, compare, classify, or justify
pointer behavior | Behavior | a structural label for observable or specified activity across conditions and time
pointer boundary | Boundary | a structural label for the declared inclusion, exclusion, or interface limit of a subject
pointer capability | Capability | a structural label for an ability available to a participant or system in context
pointer capacity | Capacity | a structural label for an available limit, amount, throughput, or ability under stated conditions
pointer claim | Claim | a structural label for an assertion whose scope, support, and status can be examined
pointer condition | Condition | a structural label for a circumstance under which a structure, rule, or result applies
pointer consequence | Consequence | a structural label for an effect or disposition associated with a condition or action
pointer constraint | Constraint | a structural label for a condition that limits admissible structures, states, or choices
pointer context | Context | a structural label for the surrounding frame in which meaning or validity is evaluated
pointer contract | Contract | a structural label for declared obligations, interfaces, guarantees, or failure conditions
pointer convention | Convention | a structural label for a declared interpretive, representational, or calculation practice
pointer criteria | Criteria | structural labels for declared standards used to judge, select, classify, or evaluate
pointer decision | Decision | a structural label for a selected disposition among alternatives under authority and criteria
pointer direction | Direction | a structural label for orientation, ordering, flow, or signed change in a declared frame
pointer domain | Domain | a structural label for the bounded subject area or admissible set in which a structure applies
pointer environment | Environment | a structural label for external surroundings relevant to a bounded subject
pointer evidence | Evidence | a structural label for observations, records, or results offered in support of a claim or decision
pointer frame | Frame | a structural label for the selected viewpoint, coordinate basis, or interpretive setting
pointer identity | Identity | a structural label for how a subject is distinguished and followed across a declared scope
pointer instrument | Instrument | a structural label for a means used to perform, mediate, or record an action
pointer interval | Interval | a structural label for a bounded span of time, quantity, order, or admissible values
pointer measure | Measure | a structural label for an operationalized quantity or indicator used in comparison or evaluation
pointer measurement | Measurement | a structural label for an observation process and its resulting quantity under a method
pointer method | Method | a structural label for a declared way of observing, transforming, evaluating, or deciding
pointer model | Model | a structural label for a bounded representation used to describe, explain, predict, or evaluate
pointer object | Object | a structural label for a participant or subject toward which an action is directed
pointer observation | Observation | a structural label for a recorded or reported result obtained under declared conditions
pointer operation | Operation | a structural label for a selected transformation or requested action
pointer outcome | Outcome | a structural label for an intended or realized result over a declared horizon
pointer policy | Policy | a structural label for a governing choice, rule set, or decision framework
pointer population | Population | a structural label for the set of subjects or cases to which an analysis refers
pointer provenance | Provenance | a structural label for the origin, custody, and transformation history of a subject or claim
pointer purpose | Purpose | a structural label for the reason, beneficiary, or desired result organizing a view
pointer quantity | Quantity | a structural label for a property expressed through magnitude, kind, unit, or comparison basis
pointer recipient | Recipient | a structural label for a participant receiving an object, message, effect, or action
pointer representation | Representation | a structural label for a selected form that stands for a subject under conventions
pointer resource | Resource | a structural label for something available, consumed, allocated, reserved, or governed
pointer result | Result | a structural label for an output, finding, state, or value produced by a process or evaluation
pointer review | Review | a structural label for an examination, forum, cadence, or disposition step
pointer revision | Revision | a structural label for a tracked change to content, configuration, interpretation, or status
pointer rule | Rule | a structural label for a declared condition-to-disposition or condition-to-consequence statement
pointer scale | Scale | a structural label for the ordered, categorical, spatial, temporal, or numerical frame of comparison
pointer scenario | Scenario | a structural label for a bounded set of conditions used to analyze or compare behavior
pointer scope | Scope | a structural label for the declared extent within which a claim, rule, action, or result applies
pointer source | Source | a structural label for an origin of authority, evidence, material, information, or influence
pointer state | State | a structural label for selected properties of a subject at a declared time and frame
pointer status | Status | a structural label for a classified condition or lifecycle disposition at a declared point
pointer subject | Subject | a structural label for the entity, system, population, or claim-bearer being considered
pointer system | System | a structural label for a bounded set of interacting components considered as a whole
pointer target | Target | a structural label for the intended recipient, destination, threshold, or object of an action
pointer time | Time | a structural label for an instant, interval, order, duration, or horizon in a declared frame
pointer uncertainty | Uncertainty | a structural label for bounded lack of knowledge, variability, or confidence in a result
pointer unit | Unit | a structural label for a measurement unit, counting basis, analysis subject, or comparison element
pointer value | Value | a structural label for a magnitude, category, preference, worth, or assigned content in context
pointer version | Version | a structural label for a declared revision or configuration identity
end-factorium-pointer-registry
